# ── robots.txt (must NOT redirect) ─────────────────────────────
# The forced /* catch-all was 301ing /robots.txt to the ACCC homepage —
# an HTML page, not a robots.txt. Google follows robots.txt redirects but
# treats a non-robots.txt destination as an unfetchable robots.txt, and then
# backs off crawling the whole host. That blocks the 301s below from ever
# being seen, and fails Search Console's Change of Address check with
# "Couldn't fetch the page". Serve the real file instead.
